# width: 120
# height: 40
# `Ctrl+Q` on a CLEAN workspace stops to ask too — the fat-finger guard.
# The box is the quit's own, with Quit / Cancel instead of the three
# buttons unsaved work gets, and Cancel holds the focus so Enter on a box
# nobody meant to raise is safe. Esc, Enter, `c` and a click on Cancel all
# leave the session exactly where it was.

write one.txt "one\n"
open one.txt
expect dirty false

key ctrl+q
expect screen contains "Quit mnml?"
expect screen contains "Nothing is unsaved. This closes mnml."
expect screen contains "Quit"
expect screen contains "Cancel"
# Nothing unsaved means nothing to save: the dirty box's buttons are not here.
expect screen lacks "Save all"
expect screen lacks "Quit anyway"

# Esc cancels; the workspace is still open.
key esc
expect screen lacks "Quit mnml?"
expect pane "one.txt"
expect screen contains "one"

# Enter lands on Cancel, because Cancel has the focus.
key ctrl+q
expect screen contains "Quit mnml?"
key enter
expect screen lacks "Quit mnml?"
expect pane "one.txt"

# `c` is Cancel's own letter.
key ctrl+q
expect screen contains "Quit mnml?"
key c
expect screen lacks "Quit mnml?"
expect pane "one.txt"

# The session is still usable after all that: the buffer still takes
# text, and Ctrl+Z puts it back so the workspace is clean again — the
# box below has to be the CLEAN one, not the unsaved-work box.
type " still here"
expect dirty true
expect screen contains " still hereone"
key ctrl+z
expect dirty false
expect screen lacks " still hereone"

# And the Quit button really is a quit. A click anywhere dismisses the
# box, so only this — the button's own row, and the app gone after it —
# tells a hit on `Quit` apart from a click that missed. x 66 is inside
# ` Quit `; the clean box's other button, Cancel, sits at 71..78.
key ctrl+q
expect screen contains "Quit mnml?"
expect screen contains "Nothing is unsaved."
expect status contains "\"quit\":false"
click 66 14
expect status contains "\"quit\":true"
